Every run gives a new scene, and passing a seed (`python3 nightscape.py 2026`) makes it reproducible — the script prints the seed after each render so you can recreate any scene you like. I tested three seeds and got a half moon, a gibbous, and a crescent, each with distinctly different ridge lines. Feel free to run it a few times, or ask me to extend it (color via ANSI codes, animated water, a sunrise mode…).
